Rule 1 (input tensor must have more than 0 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (dtype of input tensor must be in quantized dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 6
>>
Rule 3 (minimum value of input tensor must be less than maximum value)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) < max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (shape of input tensor should not be empty, i.e., at least one element)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (dtype of input tensor should not be bool or string)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 6 (for 0-dimensional tensor, the number of elements should be 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = 1
>>
Rule 7 (shape of the input tensor must be a tuple of positive integers)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 8 (if the tensor is quantized, its scale must be a positive float)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 1 <= dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) <= 6 then true
>>
Rule 9 (elements inside list of tensors must be tensors)
{v_1 : list(tensor)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : true
>>
Rule 10 (If the tensor is a list of tensors, the length of the list must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : list(tensor)} |= v_1.len > 0
